<% content_for :title, "IFS & Bipolar | Bipolar Sober" %>

<main class="ifs-bipolar-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="ifs-bipolar-hero">
    <div class="ifs-bipolar-hero-content">

      <p class="ifs-bipolar-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / BIPOLAR / PERSPECTIVES / IFS
      </p>

      <h1>
        <span>BIPOLAR</span>
        <span>THROUGH AN</span>
        <span>IFS LENS.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="ifs-bipolar-intro">
        YOU HAVE PARTS.<br>
        NONE OF THEM ARE ALL OF YOU.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 01 / THE BASIC IDEA -->
  <section class="ifs-section ifs-pink">

    <div class="ifs-section-heading">
      <p class="ifs-number">
        01 / THE BASIC IDEA
      </p>

      <h2>
        YOU ARE<br>
        NOT ONE<br>
        THING.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-copy">

      <p class="ifs-lead">
        Internal Family Systems — IFS — looks at the mind
        as containing different parts with different emotions,
        fears, needs, beliefs, and jobs.
      </p>

      <p>
        There might be a part of you that wants control.
        Another wants escape. Another gets furious.
        Another wants everybody to leave you the hell alone.
        Another desperately wants somebody to stay.
      </p>

      <p>
        Those contradictions don't necessarily mean you're fake,
        broken, or impossible to understand.
      </p>

      <p>
        They may mean different parts of you are trying to solve
        different problems.
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        A PART OF ME FEELS THIS.<br>
        THAT IS DIFFERENT FROM:<br>
        THIS IS ALL OF ME.
      </blockquote>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 02 / SELF -->
  <section class="ifs-section ifs-yellow">

    <div class="ifs-section-heading">
      <p class="ifs-number">
        02 / SELF
      </p>

      <h2>
        WHO'S<br>
        BEHIND THE<br>
        NOISE?
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-copy">

      <p class="ifs-lead">
        IFS distinguishes your parts from what it calls the Self.
      </p>

      <p>
        Self isn't another personality hiding somewhere in your head.
        It's the grounded capacity to approach your internal experience
        with qualities like curiosity, compassion, calm, clarity,
        courage, and perspective.
      </p>

      <p>
        Sometimes that perspective is easy to access.
        Sometimes everything is screaming too fucking loudly.
      </p>

      <div class="ifs-self-grid">

        <span>CURIOSITY</span>
        <span>COMPASSION</span>
        <span>CALM</span>
        <span>CLARITY</span>
        <span>COURAGE</span>
        <span>CONNECTION</span>

      </div>

      <blockquote>
        INSTEAD OF "WHAT THE FUCK IS WRONG WITH ME?"<br>
        TRY "WHAT IS HAPPENING INSIDE ME?"
      </blockquote>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 03 / PARTS -->
  <section class="ifs-section ifs-black">

    <div class="ifs-section-heading">
      <p class="ifs-number">
        03 / PARTS
      </p>

      <h2>
        EVERYBODY'S<br>
        GOT A<br>
        FUCKING JOB.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-copy">

      <p class="ifs-lead">
        IFS assumes that even behaviors you hate may have developed
        around some attempt to protect you.
      </p>

      <div class="ifs-parts">

        <div>
          <span>THE CONTROLLER</span>
          <p>
            If I control everything, maybe nothing can hurt us.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>THE ESCAPER</span>
          <p>
            If we get numb enough, maybe we won't have to feel this.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>THE ANGRY ONE</span>
          <p>
            If I attack first, nobody gets close enough to hurt us.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>THE PERFECTIONIST</span>
          <p>
            If we never fuck up, maybe nobody can reject us.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>THE IMPULSIVE ONE</span>
          <p>
            This hurts right now. Do something that changes it right now.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>THE CRITIC</span>
          <p>
            If I punish us first, maybe other people's judgment won't hurt as much.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        Understanding a protective intention doesn't mean every behavior
        is safe, healthy, or acceptable.
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        UNDERSTANDING THE PART<br>
        DOESN'T MEAN LETTING IT DRIVE.
      </blockquote>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 04 / BIPOLAR -->
  <section class="ifs-section ifs-purple">

    <div class="ifs-section-heading">
      <p class="ifs-number">
        04 / BIPOLAR
      </p>

      <h2>
        PARTS<br>
        AREN'T<br>
        EPISODES.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-copy">

      <p class="ifs-lead">
        This distinction matters.
      </p>

      <p>
        IFS is a way of understanding internal experiences.
        Bipolar disorder is a mood disorder.
      </p>

      <p>
        Mania isn't simply an IFS part.
        Depression isn't simply an IFS part.
        Psychosis isn't something you should try to explain away
        as a protective part.
      </p>

      <p>
        But mood states can affect which fears, beliefs, impulses,
        defenses, and internal conflicts become louder.
      </p>

      <p>
        IFS can offer language for exploring those experiences
        without replacing bipolar treatment or pretending everything
        happening in an episode can be solved through introspection.
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        USE THE LENS.<br>
        DON'T CONFUSE THE LENS WITH THE DIAGNOSIS.
      </blockquote>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 05 / GET CURIOUS -->
  <section class="ifs-section ifs-pink">

    <div class="ifs-section-heading">
      <p class="ifs-number">
        05 / CURIOSITY
      </p>

      <h2>
        ASK BEFORE<br>
        YOU ATTACK.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-copy">

      <p class="ifs-lead">
        Most of us are extremely good at declaring war
        on the parts of ourselves we don't like.
      </p>

      <p>
        The angry part is an asshole.
        The anxious part is annoying.
        The impulsive part ruins everything.
        The addicted part needs to shut the fuck up.
      </p>

      <p>
        IFS tries something different.
      </p>

      <div class="ifs-questions">

        <p>WHAT ARE YOU AFRAID WOULD HAPPEN IF YOU STOPPED?</p>
        <p>WHAT ARE YOU TRYING TO DO FOR ME?</p>
        <p>WHEN DID YOU LEARN THAT THIS WAS YOUR JOB?</p>
        <p>WHAT DO YOU NEED ME TO UNDERSTAND?</p>

      </div>

      <p>
        Curiosity doesn't mean obedience.
      </p>

      <p>
        You can listen to a part without doing what it wants.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 06 / UNBLENDING -->
  <section class="ifs-section ifs-yellow">

    <div class="ifs-section-heading">
      <p class="ifs-number">
        06 / UNBLENDING
      </p>

      <h2>
        STEP<br>
        BACK<br>
        A LITTLE.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-copy">

      <p class="ifs-lead">
        IFS uses the idea of "blending" for moments when a part
        becomes so strong that it feels like your entire identity.
      </p>

      <div class="ifs-unblend">

        <div>
          <span>BLENDED</span>
          <p>
            "I am completely fucking worthless."
          </p>
        </div>

        <b>→</b>

        <div>
          <span>A LITTLE SPACE</span>
          <p>
            "A part of me feels completely worthless right now."
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        That tiny change in language can create distance
        without denying what you're experiencing.
      </p>

      <p>
        The feeling is still real.
        The pain is still real.
      </p>

      <p>
        But now there is also somebody noticing it.
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        I HAVE THIS FEELING.<br>
        I AM MORE THAN THIS FEELING.
      </blockquote>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 07 / POLARIZATION -->
  <section class="ifs-section ifs-purple">

    <div class="ifs-section-heading">
      <p class="ifs-number">
        07 / POLARIZED PARTS
      </p>

      <h2>
        INTERNAL<br>
        TUG OF<br>
        WAR.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-copy">

      <p class="ifs-lead">
        Sometimes two parts are pulling in completely
        opposite directions.
      </p>

      <div class="ifs-polarized">

        <div>
          <span>ONE PART</span>
          <h3>FUCK EVERYBODY. LEAVE ME ALONE.</h3>
        </div>

        <b>VS.</b>

        <div>
          <span>ANOTHER PART</span>
          <h3>PLEASE DON'T FUCKING LEAVE ME.</h3>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        Or one part wants sobriety while another wants immediate relief.
      </p>

      <p>
        One wants stability while another misses intensity.
      </p>

      <p>
        One wants help while another hates needing anybody.
      </p>

      <p>
        Instead of deciding one side is the "real you,"
        IFS asks what each side is protecting.
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        MAYBE THE CONTRADICTION ISN'T PROOF
        THAT YOU'RE FULL OF SHIT.
      </blockquote>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 08 / COMPASSION + ACCOUNTABILITY -->
  <section class="ifs-section ifs-pink">

    <div class="ifs-section-heading">
      <p class="ifs-number">
        08 / ACCOUNTABILITY
      </p>

      <h2>
        COMPASSION<br>
        ISN'T A<br>
        FREE PASS.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-copy">

      <p class="ifs-lead">
        Understanding why a part reacted doesn't erase
        the consequences of what happened.
      </p>

      <p>
        Maybe the angry part was protecting you.
        It still may have said something cruel.
      </p>

      <p>
        Maybe the impulsive part was desperate for relief.
        The money may still be gone.
      </p>

      <p>
        Maybe your behavior happened during an episode.
        Somebody may still have been hurt.
      </p>

      <div class="ifs-accountability">

        <div>
          <span>COMPASSION</span>
          <p>
            Why did this make sense inside me?
          </p>
        </div>

        <b>+</b>

        <div>
          <span>ACCOUNTABILITY</span>
          <p>
            What happened, and what needs repair?
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <blockquote>
        I CAN UNDERSTAND WHY IT HAPPENED
        AND STILL TAKE RESPONSIBILITY FOR WHAT HAPPENED.
      </blockquote>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 09 / PRACTICE -->
  <section class="ifs-section ifs-black">

    <div class="ifs-section-heading">
      <p class="ifs-number">
        09 / PUT IT INTO PRACTICE
      </p>

      <h2>
        WHO'S<br>
        TALKING<br>
        RIGHT NOW?
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-copy">

      <p class="ifs-lead">
        When something inside you gets loud,
        you don't immediately have to fight it or obey it.
      </p>

      <div class="ifs-practice-list">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>
            <strong>NOTICE.</strong><br>
            What am I feeling, thinking, or wanting to do?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>
            <strong>CREATE SPACE.</strong><br>
            Try "a part of me feels..." instead of "I am..."
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>
            <strong>GET CURIOUS.</strong><br>
            What is this part trying to accomplish?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>
            <strong>LOOK UNDERNEATH.</strong><br>
            What is it afraid would happen if it stopped?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <p>
            <strong>DON'T AUTOMATICALLY OBEY.</strong><br>
            Understanding an urge doesn't mean acting on it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>06</span>
          <p>
            <strong>RESPOND FROM YOUR VALUES.</strong><br>
            What does the larger version of me want to do next?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>07</span>
          <p>
            <strong>KNOW WHEN THIS IS BIGGER THAN PARTS WORK.</strong><br>
            Mood episodes and serious symptoms may need outside support,
            treatment, and your bipolar care plan.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- ENDING -->
  <section class="ifs-ending">

    <div>

      <p class="ifs-ending-small">
        YOU CONTAIN A LOT OF VOICES.
      </p>

      <h2>
        NONE OF THEM<br>
        ARE THE<br>
        <span>WHOLE YOU.</span>
      </h2>

    </div>

    <div class="ifs-ending-copy">

      <p>
        The angry part isn't all of you.
      </p>

      <p>
        The scared part isn't all of you.
      </p>

      <p>
        The impulsive part isn't all of you.
      </p>

      <p>
        Even the parts you're ashamed of can be approached
        with curiosity without being given control.
      </p>

      <p>
        You can listen to what's happening inside,
        take responsibility for what happens outside,
        and remember that you're bigger than any one part.
      </p>

      <%= link_to "← BACK TO PERSPECTIVES",
          bipolar_perspectives_path,
          class: "ifs-back-button" %>

    </div>

  </section>

</main>